        {
          "_baseline_note_raises": "AUTHORISED RE-RECORD of `raises` on THIS handler only (`backend_app.routers.user.update_notif_settings`, PUT /api/notifications/settings) — TWO ADDED entries, `409` and `503`, and nothing removed or retyped. Required by NOTIF-02. THE 409 is the mandatory-alert floor: `components/NotificationPreferences.jsx` ended with \"Mandatory risk alerts (global kill switch triggers) cannot be disabled\" and rendered, directly above that sentence, the switch that disabled them. Nothing enforced the claim — readers of `notification_settings` across `backend_app` are two, both in this router, and nothing on the dispatch path reads it. Migration 073 adds `chk_notification_settings_mandatory_alerts`, and this status is what a payload refused by it now answers instead of a 500. THE 503 replaces an unguarded `.upsert().execute()`: before this, ANY write failure became a 500 with no sentence a customer could act on. NEITHER IS A NEW REFUSAL OF A LEGAL REQUEST: the request model's own validator (`NotificationEvents.mandatory_alerts_stay_on`) answers 422 first, so the 409 is reachable only when the model and the constraint disagree — which is logged at ERROR with the offending keys, because that disagreement is a defect rather than a customer mistake.",
          "decorators": [
            "router.put('/notifications/settings')"
          ],
          "handler": "update_notif_settings",
          "module": "backend_app.routers.user",
          "parameters": {
            "body": {
              "annotation": "NotificationSettingsRequest"
            },
            "supabase": {
              "annotation": "SyncClient",
              "depends_on": "get_request_supabase"
            },
            "user": {
              "annotation": "dict",
              "depends_on": "get_current_user"
            }
          },
          "raises": [
            {
              "detail_type": "computed",
              "status_code": 409
            },
            {
              "detail_type": "str",
              "status_code": 503
            }
          ],
          "returns": [
            {
              "status": "str"
            },
            {
              "status": "str"
            }
          ],
          "route_path": "/api/notifications/settings"
        }
      ],
      "method": "PUT",
      "path": "/api/notifications/settings",
      "path_template": "/api/notifications/settings",
      "resolved": true,
      "via": "api.user.updateNotificationSettings"
    },
